      "index": "58",
      "locator": "paragraph 58",
      "text": "Expansion of Idaho Medicare and Medicaid programs to create a free, universal healthcare plan for all Idahoans, with no premiums, co-pays, or deductibles, and guarantees for reproductive and gender-affirming care.",
      "sha256": "f2406c8982909d0c7fc7633432a7b584af4ea84e2affa938c2f29a8b39981ad8"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "9b34124532ba5aed3570a3bb",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "59",
      "locator": "paragraph 59",
      "text": "Idaho Medicare for All would cover all healthcare needs, including abortion, reproductive care, and transgender healthcare. Bodily autonomy should never be up for debate, and intimate healthcare decisions should be between only the patient and their doctor. This plan would include access to pregnancy-terminating drugs, hormone replacement therapy for transgender patients, and coverage for reproductive care for those who cannot conceive on their own.",
      "sha256": "3bfe68e4c297d4178b38df8598179c7ad36e57e2d27d51e134cb696529eb894a"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "f4a8db5b937de4aaf2a80d68",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "60",
      "locator": "paragraph 60",
      "text": "Every year, thousands of Idahoans go deep into medical debt, and many are forced to declare bankruptcy as a result. This debt is ultimately sold to collectors for pennies on the dollar, who are incessant and unconscionable in their attempts to collect. The State of Idaho would buy up the medical debt of qualifying Idaho residents, at which point the debt would be forgiven, saving Idahoans millions of dollars per year that they can save, or put toward other expenses like food, rent, or taking care of their families.",
      "sha256": "86ef25885b1cc94e8ddb2ce3148a0356a9e43d84c2255b413c73366f2a9e3c8d"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "fd7cd720332946d4867a540b",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "61",
      "locator": "paragraph 61",
      "text": "An end to the failed “War on Drugs” within the state of Idaho, including the decriminalization and ultimately full legalization of marijuana and cannabis products, a shifting of priorities to treat drug addiction as a health issue rather than a criminal issue, and a focus on drug education and abuse prevention.",
      "sha256": "dae8aa082a55ecb8b9775dddccc26c25e0755bb058fd32d37708ff941ab7d6ec"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "dda4dd0c15a599a74ddf82f4",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "62",
      "locator": "paragraph 62",
      "text": "Housing & Economic Security",
      "sha256": "547410706c560e31579af3680b973eea0d001e74f5dea4d14caeb9c56b46a2ae"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "1fc1aebe3748b5bbbffb9bd9",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "63",
      "locator": "paragraph 63",
      "text": "Universal Housing",
      "sha256": "9881c67d492a6ffbafb6e2addabf9001ff5d4322db77b09ba881c5f69a461baa"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "8de81d1433b2441b302020aa",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "64",
      "locator": "paragraph 64",
      "text": "College for All",
      "sha256": "2d3e125fa24d0517f7f55ffdd0a1f6ccbc474c135a2701a7616aa2b17551b236"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "185260e8d2cc626c0cc4a919",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "65",
      "locator": "paragraph 65",
      "text": "Increase Idaho’s Minimum Wage",
      "sha256": "6861008618dba2d4b46614622f849c1c5c388e7ab4759f404cb704eb07fcef8e"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "c05ca2a4d337850137110ab7",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "66",
      "locator": "paragraph 66",
      "text": "Labor and Right to Work",
      "sha256": "2b0a62087be0553668479ae54b97b4f63c38bc825eefef00a333429b44c901cd"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "7d069827b87098871b6dd97b",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "67",
      "locator": "paragraph 67",
      "text": "Support for Workers and",
      "sha256": "3512d6232d575700ec187d7c6f43018884858d0deae83061c90e2ced3b620ceb"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "5d134d2cd14ea2da650d4007",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "68",
      "locator": "paragraph 68",
      "text": "Working Families",
      "sha256": "a2133ad6fcccfd0d8352e3bf381440e21ee83443f35a681034c2198e2144e046"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "f27117713a677d25f2bff0b1",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "69",
      "locator": "paragraph 69",
      "text": "Work From Home Telework Initiative",
      "sha256": "4ea148217752cf7297d49b9a281e47366f395427b73bb68a5ee71fd0e5d43296"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "84f6db2e95a85fac93a9ae2f",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "70",
      "locator": "paragraph 70",
      "text": "Establish statewide rent controls tied to state minimum wage and national housing per-diem rate. Guaranteed right to counsel for all tenants. Public investment in building quality multi-income social housing and an expansion of programs to place those most in need with suitable, high-quality, and well-maintained housing.",
      "sha256": "864e1bb8b004e3b7b57d303253a19c5d81ca6fe1ef5635e8872e84f1a6933376"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "b1e5c5bbdea7585d88e3350b",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "71",
      "locator": "paragraph 71",
      "text": "Revamping Idaho’s K-12 education system to better prepare students for college, and restructure the Idaho high school curriculum to meet the requirements of a 2-year associate of arts degree so that all students graduating from Idaho schools will have a head start on college, whether they remain in Idaho or not. Expansion of the Idaho LAUNCH program to cover more post-secondary education and greater dollar amounts, with the ultimate goal of creating a universal free college system for Idaho residents.",
      "sha256": "4f33a87e81eaa45f964874be0f6957b8d3e563ced2aab628fc1132bc21e3a59e"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "ea95d29504e158cde8c18059",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "72",
      "locator": "paragraph 72",
      "text": "An immediate increase of the Idaho minimum wage to $15 an hour, with further step increases planned through 2035 before tying the minimum wage to the Consumer Price Index.",
      "sha256": "792745a4d35118c938fb806c2f30b5e784ef094cc44f0cc2788a5db9fa75e987"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "0e5dc6e8785aa829489c189f",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "73",
      "locator": "paragraph 73",
      "text": "A repeal of Idaho’s “Right to Work” status, so that workers can have a fair chance at unionizing if they so choose, as well as establishing a non-interference and neutrality commitment for public sector unions on behalf of the Idaho state government.",
      "sha256": "7651bd5650136f18049f1b4cb3b312f74f9af82d80dff5771484d3c8fd8ff161"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "af795d891ee448b83acd2b01",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "74",
      "locator": "paragraph 74",
      "text": "Protecting the current ratio of journeymen to apprentices in all trades, and vetoing any legislation that would take the power of determining these ratios away from organized labor.",
      "sha256": "2a0a9b85c5c8b12d3aad265c973fe35d16ad01c8ee0f7890fc86ac8cc71d1fe7"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "3ae1551e2e1a2a8d1c5ff484",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "75",
      "locator": "paragraph 75",
      "text": "Paid family leave for all workers, and free public universal childcare and pre-K as an expansion of the Idaho Public School system.",
      "sha256": "f4fb6aba764be5108f04ad87ff3675db021f150b90f1c65c221f79a0482c8cb7"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "e1000a380f1482fbf1a6b192",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "76",
      "locator": "paragraph 76",
      "text": "A concerted push to make “work from home” telework the preferred and encouraged method of employment for all applicable Idaho jobs, and to expand the capacity and availability of high-speed internet throughout the state to support this initiative.",
      "sha256": "ccea84ff0411593ce34abde0e66bca519d66d6cd569a9e37cf4e92f4fefbcfb8"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "2e728c9bc10bdf77c933494c",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "77",
      "locator": "paragraph 77",
      "text": "Agriculture & Safety",
      "sha256": "ce868a17814015e5cf0247f281107d98328ad4b7f7f106664e80e2deef0eda6f"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "6fb7ecbf6119aaad3f8caed1",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "78",
      "locator": "paragraph 78",
      "text": "Small Farm Support and",
      "sha256": "f54d83304d689007e33591fb9e3a5000b19db9ea881497fd2af2b9efb0d1f448"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "118293a4389edd01093242e6",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "79",
      "locator": "paragraph 79",
      "text": "“First-Time Farmer” Initiative",
      "sha256": "336695e7aac97b0896073910880284843bebf99581a9f8b4e7f530de64b7d31a"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "16982b1b06fd3bc2b983e366",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "80",
      "locator": "paragraph 80",
      "text": "Public Lands and Freedom to Roam",
      "sha256": "421820c985fbbcd4fa9260f109e0842c2f27323b37812aec339b28adc4c1e058"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "f9a37871a35f0647dcedf528",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "81",
      "locator": "paragraph 81",
      "text": "Universal Hunter’s Education,",
      "sha256": "46bce305428477557e77fbebbba5fa979109b676c9987f6d798c4cf1fb4c51ab"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "7efdce949155bcd0c4b16c0b",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "82",
      "locator": "paragraph 82",
      "text": "Gun Safety, and Permitting",
      "sha256": "a8ec12facfd98f2509d9008def76033dbc64b0da7047c87f74be4ec495d6cfd4"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "1143f2b02a71bf61a0110457",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "83",
      "locator": "paragraph 83",
      "text": "Increased state grant funding for small farms operated by families or individuals, and for first-time farmers looking to buy land and start new farms or those trying to redevelop existing family farms. Idaho’s legacy as a rural, agricultural state is under attack by factory farms and large-scale industrial farming, but by creating incentives for the next generation of Idaho’s small farmers, we can preserve our heritage while adapting for the food needs of the future.",
      "sha256": "342f8befd88d9e393061a73ec47bc872695992065a174c5a18b296ba659ab8e7"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "4735a869e187ace286504974",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "84",
      "locator": "paragraph 84",
      "text": "A full moratorium on any sale of public lands currently owned by the State of Idaho, as well as an initiative to reclaim public lands sold under previous administrations. A further effort to purchase or otherwise legally obtain private land that has been abandoned, or that may serve the public good, which would then be converted into nature space or public housing. Enacting a “Freedom to Roam” policy for all Idaho public lands and right-of-way, so that Idaho’s natural beauty can be enjoyed by all, and not hoarded behind private roads or fences.",
      "sha256": "3762dde7c33e3ced353d66e9ec4e4c9b3dd02c4a73e4a33d9a48241772a6bb95"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "d8ab52a4afa81789e084f917",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "85",
      "locator": "paragraph 85",
      "text": "An expansion to current gun safety and hunter’s education courses to include first aid and CPR certification, mental health first aid training, de-escalation, and emergency management training, so that Idaho gun owners are trained on not only how to utilize their rights under the Second Amendment, but also understand the responsibility of gun ownership and have the additional training and resources to help others in times of emergency. Funding would be allocated to make this program free of charge to any Idaho resident who wants to utilize it.",
      "sha256": "5f7d606a8f60ce4c128dfa12cc465feffce910e1de4d1d4e46742d661874d166"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "91df615f880a43b9802a94f4",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "86",
      "locator": "paragraph 86",
      "text": "Good Governance",
      "sha256": "17bdd88bd4c347852f6f818d21da5fec6ce6f15999ea832b817de6bb6c219711"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "4614b5addab37e412b0a12ce",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "87",
      "locator": "paragraph 87",
      "text": "Term Limits",
      "sha256": "eb420f24e1612f03f2493b193dacc295ba79f035c38176635b4ddf78cf84fc68"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "378d32930e2dcd4867198888",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "88",
      "locator": "paragraph 88",
      "text": "Add the Words",
      "sha256": "6198cbfa513ea19d8ad9c25dd7485c7645764e340d90727f709deca1147349de"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "68d9bc130d502c313145e180",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "89",
      "locator": "paragraph 89",
      "text": "Term limits for all state and local Idaho government positions, for a maximum of two terms (consecutive or nonconsecutive) in a person’s life. Those currently serving in their second term or terms beyond a second term may finish those terms, but will not be eligible for any further terms.",
      "sha256": "9857e0e3287af3b808b583c8127bd79ff42482a4dddd2c519e996859aa156de8"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "3625d652a3abea524127c784",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "90",
      "locator": "paragraph 90",
      "text": "An amendment to the Idaho Human Rights Act to add the words “sexual orientation” and “gender identity”, and enshrine protections for LGBTQ individuals at the state level.",
      "sha256": "4258f98735ede47023b79e79457936d7556b505da2c9a066eeed488673063b53"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "cec09efe385c5821d2a43171",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "91",
      "locator": "paragraph 91",
      "text": "Innovation & Industry",
      "sha256": "1d5e7ccc5eec7b7e40243c3e00cdea5d74b0f78692dafd08cdda43186467c678"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "38e1594e80aeb8748a05ccc3",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "92",
      "locator": "paragraph 92",
      "text": "Energy Independence Initiative",
      "sha256": "a92cedd029fe8454cb173e328c71fba97803a39f8c6adcea7374e06f6994711f"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "3a3073b166ae2d5132ff8655",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "93",
      "locator": "paragraph 93",
      "text": "Science Industry Development",
      "sha256": "2d14cb5d680b76367a33b53c6f6b7ff48256234daae0c3306fe78e5c3a070e48"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "01aab146499640189285fbac",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "94",
      "locator": "paragraph 94",
      "text": "Right to Repair",
      "sha256": "3555f6d6b10676c46f2b7c356d6e64adcac9f6faa1c061186e3bddb494186f3a"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "11bb3e50775a8ffd7a7e8cb9",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "95",
      "locator": "paragraph 95",
      "text": "Idaho Public Transit Trust Fund",
      "sha256": "e617c95176ddc3d7cde6f31e23eda797f7abc34b1439a1b6f2830256768269fe"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "2c35dc91fe1b741e2b3443bb",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "96",
      "locator": "paragraph 96",
      "text": "Funding for the Arts and Humanities",
      "sha256": "2f7262f37e61eb1cd697f7c2261ffc46ae9bf3cfa11b44865c9d101d2220d613"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "6a70f7f9d904d5b137884684",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "97",
      "locator": "paragraph 97",
      "text": "Changes to Idaho’s power generation regulations to make home ownership of wind, solar, and geothermal energy production systems more accessible, feasible, and affordable, with the goal of empowering Idahoans to create their own sustainable power generation for off-grid use, and to decentralize the state power grid by making it easier to sell excess generation.",
      "sha256": "5a40891f9d090e0b5b3b484df043032b2f318a0323b80d9c4ca4bd4781257de2"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "ec866337329c3f62c0a54fc0",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "98",
      "locator": "paragraph 98",
      "text": "Creating new opportunities to fund development in Idaho’s science and technology sector, both to attract existing technology companies to expand or relocate to Idaho, and to encourage Idaho STEM graduates to start new businesses locally. The next major breakthroughs in science and technology should be made in Idaho, and this will only happen if we invest in the future.",
      "sha256": "23671b3e689fde6e16dc5545244183256066a8688660271e59433bf2a93fd2d4"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "1baa012ccdbdc77866d6d523",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "99",
      "locator": "paragraph 99",
      "text": "Enshrining “Right to Repair” into Idaho law for all property, but with particular focus on farm equipment, electronics and software, and automobiles. For too long, Idahoans have been forced into uncooperative and predatory terms when trying to repair or modify their own property, in the form of overzealous warranties or restrictions from the manufacturer. Whether it’s a farm tractor or a personal computer, if you paid for it, you should have the right to do with it as you see fit.",
      "sha256": "597f62d6f34f08805f3632e6c12fd0ac3fd52df901914c02430690302bc69ea7"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "33b9c94b4e70ad122082a5be",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "100",
      "locator": "paragraph 100",
      "text": "A trust fund to be created with the sole purpose of building an investment trust, which will then be used to fund public transit operations, administration, and capital projects in the state, and act as match for federal transit funds. The Trust will be funded by adding a $10 fee to all vehicle registrations in the state of Idaho, which will be pooled and invested for a period of 10 years from the date of the fund’s creation before a portion of the fund’s annual interest earnings will be made available as public transit grant funds managed by ITD.",
      "sha256": "3d7809dfabe0c86aac64a6d965a71f0008e6e30c987125c2446176c784dfe722"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "61658cbc45b9c51bd969e357",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "101",
      "locator": "paragraph 101",
      "text": "Establish a state grant program for Idaho-based artists of all kinds, increase funding for public arts and humanities education, and create a cabinet-level Secretary of the Arts position to oversee and encourage development in Idaho’s arts and entertainment industry.",
      "sha256": "23e32ac0f192d0e2555882674d3ad2a29c74245ce936cd0ac0720122df4c5ef9"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "839a799ef28589f64a6b867f",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "102",
      "locator": "paragraph 102",
      "text": "Want to learn about Maxine? Read more here",
      "sha256": "268b40f396a900da053ff2a4e09e6ed715cae8b428ec76336458c7a6e9875f2b"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "e392be1cd656005b014bb459",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "103",
      "locator": "paragraph 103",
      "text": "Feeling inspired to help? Donate here",
      "sha256": "4a3e882e086ebaa5d4097178119532ce426a974b372454bd00cb4e46340b6a47"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "0e01011ba57068453d298639",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "104",
      "locator": "paragraph 104",
      "text": "Want to hear more from Maxine? Read more here",
      "sha256": "a701ddc16dd04b7a9a7378d8b64d882f62d1b766ec4268c5b7841c303138102e"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "d20ccbc212e40ee5bbac585c",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "105",
      "locator": "paragraph 105",
      "text": "Paid for by the Committee to Elect Maxine Durand.",
      "sha256": "f75835a18a31fda6bbf9757a6ad7bb9ceff1c4cadc0cec27808ddb3b105a95e2"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "3f442f19aa9e1e1d9a435b98",
      "document_id": "replacement-durand-archive",
      "segment_kind": "paragraph",
      "index": "106",
